  "prefLabel": "Ed 1117.06 Dispute Resolution Procedures",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ed 1117.06 Dispute Resolution Procedures.\n\n(a) If a liable school district has not been identified or has refused to assume responsibility for carrying out provisions set forth in Ed 1117, unless such court ordered residential placement is in a health care facility, residential school or state institution as defined in RSA 193:27, the school district in which the child has been placed outside the home by DCYF shall identify, evaluate or otherwise provide FAPE to the child with a disability.\n\n(b) In all cases where there is a dispute regarding the identification of the liable school district, either school district may seek resolution from a court of competent jurisdiction or as otherwise provided by law.\n\nSource. (see Revision Note at chapter heading for Ed 1100) #9197, eff 6-28-08; ss by #12141, eff 3-24-17",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ed1100.html"
